    "description": "The 2nd month of the Korean year is the month of 풍신/영등신 the god of wind. They are often described as grandmother gods of the winds\n\nDuring this month, it was believed that the grandmother gods of the winds came to visit. People would pray and do rituals to ask the wind gods for protection from destructive winds\n\nWinds can be refreshing, dry, gentle, fierce and destructive. They can come from the mountains and oceans. In the philosophy/practice of 풍수 pungsu (literally “wind & water”), wind is one of two deciding factors of how one reads and interprets the energies of the land, a home, a city, etc. \n\nThis new moon in Pisces brings about quite a wind. Gusts may threaten to push us over, or blow us far away from our goals and destinations. Huge shifts are coming. Be strong, flexible and consistent! \n\nHappy 초하루 choharu everyone! It’s already the 1st day of the 2nd month of the year of the snake 🐍",
