    "description": "Let’s be honest \n\nWe live most of our lives not knowing what truly lies ahead. We may assume what’s coming next based on things like our experiences, data patterns, and advice from community\n\nWhen things happen in a predictable manner that meets our expectations for the future, we feel secure and assured. We feel that we can see clearly and we know what lies ahead\n\nWhen things don’t go as expected, it’s easy to start questioning what we thought we knew. We might feel things are really unclear, and we may even feel overwhelmed by the sudden change in perspective \n\nBut really, whether things are expected or unexpected, we never truly know what lies ahead. We do, however, decide how we meet that truth \n\nDo we meet it with fear? Curiosity? Respect?Arrogance? Denial? \n\nDo we fight? Fawn? Freeze? Run? \n\nThere’s so many ways to meet this truth, and we can meet it in any combination of ways at different times in our lives\n\nWhat is incredibly helpful in this life long journey of not knowing what comes next, is community 🤝\n\nSo who’s in your community? \n\nFriends, family, pets, ancestors, spirits, deities? Co-workers, chosen family, online communities, wild animal friends? That one lady who walks with you to the bus stop? A stranger who donated to help you? ✨\n\nPic 1 - me in black vest and off white long sleeve offering incense at the shrine \nPic 2 - incense ash standing tall and unbroken \nPic 3 - spilled rice grains next to a bowl of rice and coins on a traditional Korean fold-out table",
